From c31ad9eb64ab5328facbbda2cb61e8e4dd151219 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rick Mark-Penwell <rickmark@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:32:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH v1 1/3] Add a pthread-based PGSemaphore implementation and
 --enable-appstore

The macOS App Sandbox denies the whole System V IPC family to a
sandboxed process: shmget(), shmat(), semget() and semop() all fail
with EPERM.  src/template/darwin and meson.build select System V
semaphores on macOS, because sem_init() is unimplemented there and
named POSIX semaphores cost a file descriptor per backend per
semaphore, so a server built for the sandbox has no semaphore
implementation it can use.

Add src/backend/port/pthread_sema.c: a counting semaphore made of a
PTHREAD_PROCESS_SHARED mutex, a condition variable and a counter,
living in the main shared memory segment like the unnamed POSIX
variant does.  It needs no kernel object name and no descriptors.
Waits are not interruptible, which matches the existing
implementations.

Add a configure option, --enable-appstore (-Dappstore=true with
Meson), off by default, which defines APPSTORE and selects the pthread
semaphores.  It changes nothing in a build that does not ask for it.
A following commit makes the shared memory code honour APPSTORE too,
so that such a build creates no System V object at all.

Discussion: https://postgr.es/m/a90b5411-705f-4286-bd81-a26c520a6cfb%40technowledgy.de
---
